  "title": "Discovery Engine: Notebook Search Scoping & Feedback Detail",
  "summary": "Discovery Engine now offers granular control over federated searches by allowing you to restrict data stores to specific notebooks. Additionally, new options for partial and prefix field matching are available, and conversational feedback can now include more detailed context like step sequence numbers and trajectory IDs.",
  "details": "Developers can now define an optional `notebooks` array within `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaDataStoreFederatedSearchConfigNotebooklmConfig` (and its `v1alpha` counterpart) to precisely scope federated searches to a list of notebook resource names. This enhances data governance and relevance. For `v1alpha` users, `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaFieldConfig` gains `partialMatchableOption` and `prefixMatchableOption` enums, providing finer control over how search fields are matched. In `v1beta`, the `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaFeedback` schema now recognizes `GOOGLE_AGENTSPACE_DESKTOP` as a feedback source, and `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaFeedbackConversationInfo` includes new `stepSeqNum` (int64) and `trajectoryId` (string) fields, enabling more detailed tracking of conversational agent interactions. A minor clarification was also made to the description of the `GRACE_PERIOD` state in `LicenseConfig`.",
